{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/657585-2e-alternative-incentives-for-carthians","id":657585,"title":"[2e] Alternative Incentives for Carthians","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-09T03:35:13-07:00","id":657585,"title":"[2e] Alternative Incentives for Carthians","content":"I'm looking into creating a Requiem game, and while I am not really a fan of the Carthians, I want to explore my options before banning them outright. This might be the first of a few Carthian-centric thread as I get more information and inspiration. <br /> <br /> That said, if I am torn on Carthians as a whole, I have no such conflict about Carthian Law. I hate it, Sam-I-Am, and I would very much like ideas for alternative incentives and mechanical edges that I could offer to prospective Carthian players instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T04:03:23-07:00","id":657627,"title":"","content":"What precisely irks you about Carthian Law? If we can boil it down to a single issue there might be a simple fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T11:56:28-07:00","id":658231,"title":"","content":"Even without Carthian Law, the Carthians have some pretty killer Merits. In 1e they had a lot of unique Devotions as well, bringing some of them back could work. There's even a Devotion Experimenter Merit in the Secrets of the Covenants preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:38:04-07:00","id":658342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/657585-2e-alternative-incentives-for-carthians?p=657627#post657627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What precisely irks you about Carthian Law? If we can boil it down to a single issue there might be a simple fix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much everything about it. I don't particularly like the effects, but what bugs me most is honestly the question of metaphysics: I have yet to come across a reason why they would work at all that I like, let alone one that explains why it specifically works with Carthians and only Carthians. I heavily dislike the idea when it came out in their covenant book when it seemed like a mandated thing to give all covenants a blood sorcery equivalent, and I heavily dislike it now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:58:20-07:00","id":658425,"title":"","content":"Then don't use Carthian Law. There's a nice alternative in the Tokyo section for their Carthian-equivalent. Plus, there's all the social-benefit merits. As for why you include them? Politics. Vampire is heavily invested in political games, and there's that much less drama and plot hooks if you ban entire covenants from the game (not necessarily the same thing as being banned from the city - invasion plots are quite interesting plot hooks). <br /> <br /> As for why they work like they do? Well, I describe each of the covenant sorceries in terms of the other supernaturals and their magics. You have ceremonial magics, necromancy, techno-miracles, shamanism, and pledge magic. Oaths work like pledge magic, Theban are angelic techno-miracles, Cruac is shamanistic, the Ordo's alchemy is ceremonial, and the Carthian Law is necromantic. It uses an Underworld channel that relies on personal belief that necromantically alters how things work. So, that's my explanation - its works like GtSE magic. <br /> <br /> I have a standard plot hook involved, tied into the multiple-origin theory of clans based on this, and stealing and adapting others into the Curse. Its a bit crossover-y, but that's how I construct my world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T16:02:18-07:00","id":658576,"title":"","content":"I'd be inclined to cut back the benefits of the other covenants, or increase the associated difficulties with membership where that's not possible. I'm not personally a great fan of giving factions incentives and bonuses beyond the fluff of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T19:39:24-07:00","id":658822,"title":"","content":"I hate Carthian's because i think they're hypocrites but i would hate to see a whole covenant stripped from a game. They draw a really cool parallel to the Invictus and gives players another option. More options make for a more in depth games 7/11 times (made that up btw feel free to quote me). Don't like Carthian Law? hide it and bury it 300 feet below the earth. If you do end up with a player as a Carthian they have plenty of other tricks and tools are their finger tips no love lost.<br /> <br /> So Keep carthians, toss carthian law?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T06:05:00-07:00","id":659294,"title":"","content":"Don't be bullied into using mechanics and themes you think are inappropriate or detract from the themes you want to highlight in the name of accommodating all the desires of your players or just because the book makes them a default presentation. Too many choices stifles your creativity. Instead of working with what you have or trying to get what you need/want, you spend your time going back and forth trying to decide the optimal choice for what you want to accomplish or whether or not you should dial back a power or go full bore. This is compounded when you make those same options available to PCs, who may well find a use for a power you overlooked because you didn't care much for it in the first place. You stated you dislike the mechanics and don't care either way for the themes the Carthians endorse so they aren't really a viable choice. Throw them away.<br /> <br /> If you don't like them and don't feel like incorporating their merits (I consider Carthian Law to be cheesier than the Guile's handcuffs exploit myself.) then don't use them. If you want Club Subversive as an element whose purpose is to disrupt the status quo then make a group of dissatisfied members of (insert apex covenant here) in league with a few unaligned as agitators. Decide a few signature tactics they'll use to get what they want or disrupt rivals and engineer a few merits or devotions from that. That makes them actually relevant to your setting with abilities that work in a way that's explained in a fashion more to your liking rather than relying on some oblique pseudo-mystical concept of statism-always-supercedes-everything that is Carthian Law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T03:12:40-07:00","id":661726,"title":"","content":"So, straw poll, if you were joining a vampire game as a Carthian PC, would you feel in anyway penalized or that the other covenants had an unfair advantage if the only change was straight up removal of Carthian Law? Interested to hear your thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T04:54:24-07:00","id":661790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/657585-2e-alternative-incentives-for-carthians?p=661726#post661726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, straw poll, if you were joining a vampire game as a Carthian PC, would you feel in anyway penalized or that the other covenants had an unfair advantage if the only change was straight up removal of Carthian Law? Interested to hear your thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I don't know if I'd call it penalized, since everything is measured by OOC experience resources. But I would definately feel that it was unfair. Every one else gets shiny toys on top of social merits. Why would I play a Carthian, then? Yes, ideally, we play what's a fun and engaging character irregardless of mechanics. However, I can just as easily have just as engaging and fun of a character in the Invictus or Ordo Dracul as the Carthian Movement with better benefits, and only minor tweaks to the character. And then, I'd still have just as fun of a character with more options to choose from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T04:59:15-07:00","id":661792,"title":"","content":"On principle, yeah. Personally I don't think I'd use most of the carthian law merits so I wouldn't mind in that regard, but I probably wouldn't play a carthian character in that game because it's clear the ST doesn't want carthian characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T05:54:35-07:00","id":661830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but I probably wouldn't play a carthian character in that game because it's clear the ST doesn't want carthian characters. </div> </div> </div>I think thenagain hit the gist of the problem. Is a clear flag or red sign that my character is not going to be suported.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T08:41:37-07:00","id":661963,"title":"","content":"I'd be pretty miffed. I'm still not quite sure why you don't like Carthian Law, either. You said something about metaphysics, but I didn't interpret Carthian merits as magical at all. It's just the Carthian ability to gather popular support. No other Covenant bothers with popular support. They're all hierarchies. CL just highlights the comparatively communal nature of Carthians compared to any other Covenant. It's the support structure they've spent centuries putting into place. Crones instead spent centuries developing Cruac. The Sancum spent centuries developing Theban Sorcery. The Invictus spent centuries developing their social hierarchies and oaths and rules. A vampire could probably mimic some of Carthian Law with a whole lot of political and social rolls and favors given and such, but the Carthian social organization allows for it with just the merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T09:45:10-07:00","id":662016,"title":"","content":"Well, the Carthian Law is pretty much magic. Poachers that throw up blood and have black lips can't be explained as anything but magic. Maybe a supernatural expression of the communal willpower of the Movement as a kind of meta-Discipline, but definitely not non-magical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T13:29:06-07:00","id":662130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/657585-2e-alternative-incentives-for-carthians?p=662016#post662016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poachers that throw up blood and have black lips can't be explained as anything but magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they're just that hardcore.<br /> <br /> But yeah the Carthian laws merits explicitly say they lend some 'metaphysical weight' to Kindred laws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T13:44:22-07:00","id":662139,"title":"","content":"Well, then it's still not any different than the Invictus putting metaphysical weight behind their oaths, so I still don't see why Carthians are the only problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T13:49:45-07:00","id":662147,"title":"","content":"Some folks do have a problem with both Carthian Law and Invictus Oaths. Something about not liking that every Covenant has some form of blood sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T13:55:59-07:00","id":662175,"title":"","content":"It might have something to do with not liking the Carthians in the first place, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T14:36:05-07:00","id":662212,"title":"","content":"Yeah, because if that's the problem why are Blood Oaths ok and Carthian Law not? Say, KirbyJerusalem, why don't you have the same problem with the Invictus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T17:59:35-07:00","id":662487,"title":"","content":"Well, first, I'm not in love with the Invictus Oaths, but I find them workable. The main reason is that the Invictus Oaths are natural extensions of both the covenant fluff and the metaphysics shown in the setting - the Invictus are all about hierarchy and creating webs of social obligation, and they enforce that through the Blood. Like Cruac, Theban Sorcery, and the Coils/Scales, it all comes back to the Blood. I like that, that feels right and it falls in line with how the Kindred's more mystical powers have been shown to work.<br /> <br /> Carthian Law, meanwhile...doesn't. The clanbook gives a multiple choice reason why the magic works (and I don't like a single one) and the 2e core doesn't even touch on it, There's no reason why a bunch of vampires caring about the law gives it magical enforcement, and there's no reason why this power in particular only belongs to those vampires that call themselves &quot;Carthians&quot; - no one had the power before, and there's no explanation given why the newest, most secular covenant somehow developed a magic system of their own. On top of that, 2e takes a lot of effort to push the &quot;revolutionary&quot; aspects of the covenant, which makes it especially dissonant why they and only they are the power behind the laws of the domain. On top of THAT, I really don't like the effects.<br /> <br /> So yeah, top to bottom, I don't like Carthian Law.<br /> <br /> (Straw poll is still open, by the by.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 09-13-2015, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T03:17:28-07:00","id":662863,"title":"","content":"Hmm, as far as the whole problem of how it works goes, where you see a jarring incongruity in the setting I see a potential plot hook. How <i>can</i> the Carthians be doing this? It makes no sense. What the <i>hell</i> did they make a deal with?<br /> <br /> They're revolutionaries. I can see them consorting with beings of questionable motive to get their way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T04:00:52-07:00","id":662892,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt; (Straw poll is still open, by the by.) &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>would you feel in anyway penalized or that the other covenants had an unfair advantage if the only change was straight up removal of Carthian Law? Interested to hear your thoughts. </i><br /> <br /> Not in the slightest.<br /> <br /> Claiming I don't have access to the same powers and merits as everyone else or that it removes plot hooks is false dichtomy. Certain choices, once pursued or ignored make other plot hooks no longer viable. And if I wanted my character to have blood magic or coils, instead of whining and bitching that I can't magically steal a power through Carthian Law or ruin the game for everyone else by magically cancelling out the use of their powers and merits, I'd make my character have the requisite 1 status and buy the power, just like someone playing a member of that covenant has to do. Or buy a mentor from that covenant who can help get me what I want. Oh no... I created plot hooks that entail playing out the inevitable consequences of multiple loyalties or opened up the possibility of learning some of the motivations of another covenant, put myself at a starting point to begin a long term campaign to bring down that covenant, or potentially expose my mentor to accusations of corruption, sedition, or treason.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the entire reason the Carthian Movement is supposed to exist in the first place is because the other covenants have an unfair advantage (whatever that means) and they wish to change that. If the entire chronicle starts with Carthians having the ability to mystically eject people from clans and covenants they don't even belong to, degenerating political opponents into revenants by magically stripping away their blood potency, and arbitrarily cancelling out disciplines, then as active perpetuators of the status quo, they are the problem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T07:58:01-07:00","id":663134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/657585-2e-alternative-incentives-for-carthians?p=662892#post662892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. And if I wanted my character to have blood magic or coils, instead of whining and bitching that I can't magically steal a power through Carthian Law or ruin the game for everyone else by magically cancelling out the use of their powers and merits, I'd make my character have the requisite 1 status and buy the power, just like someone playing a member of that covenant has to do. Or buy a mentor from that covenant who can help get me what I want.</div> </div> </div> </div> Gee, somebody else doesn't like the Carthians. While I agree the one merit that lets you join other covenants without penalty is odd, it doesn't work like you've suggest, and you're grossly misrepresenting the rest of the Carthian abilities. No, they don't negate another's power.<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"> Let's not make comments about other forumites please. Darksider.</span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the entire reason the Carthian Movement is supposed to exist in the first place is because the other covenants have an unfair advantage (whatever that means) and they wish to change that. </div> </div> </div> Slightly wrong. The Movement exists because they want to challenge the status quo and update Kindred society based on modern mortal practices. They are pushing for change, leveraging every social and physical advantage they can muster to that end. There's nothing about the Carthians that suggests that other covenants have an unfair advantage other than change being difficult due to inertia and static elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 09-13-2015, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T08:31:44-07:00","id":663161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/657585-2e-alternative-incentives-for-carthians?p=662863#post662863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, as far as the whole problem of how it works goes, where you see a jarring incongruity in the setting I see a potential plot hook. How <i>can</i> the Carthians be doing this? It makes no sense. What the <i>hell</i> did they make a deal with?<br /> <br /> They're revolutionaries. I can see them consorting with beings of questionable motive to get their way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a really interesting line of discussion, but kind of off-topic for this thread. Would anyone object if we started a separate thread for general Carthian Law discussion and kept this one focused on advising Kirby on alternative advantages for Carthians in their games?<br /> <br /> As for Kirby's question, I would honestly not be too bothered if the ST in a game I played banned Carthian Law. Carthians have plenty of other Merits unique to their Covenant, and I'm never bothered by an ST saying &quot;X, Y, and Z Merits aren't appropriate for the theme and mood of this chronicle.&quot; I would hope, if there was a particular Carthian Law Merit that I felt was especially important for my character to have as part of the concept, that the ST would be willing to discuss the matter and consider making an exception, even if it meant modifying the exact details of the Merit to make it fit their chronicle. But in general, I have no problem with an ST saying &quot;hey guys, don't take [such and such power], I don't think it suits this chronicle.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, Thorbes makes a good point that banning a Covenant's unique advantage entirely is kind of a red flag that the ST might just not like the Covenant, and would make me consider playing a different Covenant. Offering some other advantage to compensate would be an appreciated gesture to make it clear it's the power you dislike, not the Covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-13-2015, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T13:24:19-07:00","id":663427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/657585-2e-alternative-incentives-for-carthians?p=663161#post663161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is a really interesting line of discussion, but kind of off-topic for this thread. Would anyone object if we started a separate thread for general Carthian Law discussion and kept this one focused on advising Kirby on alternative advantages for Carthians in their games?</div> </div> </div> </div>I say go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T16:33:26-07:00","id":663543,"title":"","content":"The law changes with time and the Carthians embrace sociopolitical change so Carthian Law fits thematically. Any alternative would face similar problems. How does it work? Why do only Carthians have it? I always considered the advantage the Carthians have to be cooperation and mutual protection as long as you pay your dues. Some Carthian Law doesn't work well unless Carthians are in charge, or not.<br /> <br /> Since I don't see a way to provide Carthians advantages that others can't have and aren't going to run into the same problems as Carthian Law, I would suggest changing the setting to give Carthians an edge. Maybe the local Carthians have an alliance with werewolves or mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T16:40:03-07:00","id":663545,"title":"","content":"I mean, do you really need to have the Carthians at all? If you don't like them and none of your players have an invested interest in playing one, could it be that there's simply no presence of that Covenant in your city? You don't have to include everything, and is possibly better to not include them at all if you dislike them so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T19:45:50-07:00","id":663780,"title":"","content":"They're an extremely useful element to have, politically speaking. They're politically active but often in direct opposition to the &quot;establishment&quot; covenants like the Invictus and, to a lesser extent, the LS. Even if I went HOG WILD and decided to ban them as a playable option entirely (which again, is not something I'm going to do lightly) I'd still probably have a small but significant section of Carthian NPCs.<br /> <br /> Also, even if -I- personally dislike the Carthians somewhat, I plan on probably offering them as a playable option, and if anyone bites then I want them to be a fun, engaging option, which is why I'm still open to ideas for alternative incentives than Carthian Law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T05:03:37-07:00","id":664107,"title":"","content":"Well, then what about bonus Merits? Select a bunch of Social Merits and let them get their (Status: Carthian) dots in them. Not as flat, here take these free Merit dots, but maybe getting puntual access to them, say, once per chapter?<br /> <br /> EDIT: also you don't really need the Carthians to get a competing political faction. Specially versus the Invictus wich is the usual one everybody thinks about. You can play the Invictus angle of protectors of the Masquerade and sort of secret police/mob enforcers instead of old aristocracy. Lancea Sanctum can have plenty of lay high ranking members to act as a political faction oposing the Invictus (even if they are said to mostly work toghether). There's plenty of posibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 09-14-2015, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T05:30:34-07:00","id":664134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/657585-2e-alternative-incentives-for-carthians?p=664107#post664107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, then what about bonus Merits? Select a bunch of Social Merits and let them get their (Status: Carthian) dots in them. Not as flat, here take these free Merit dots, but maybe getting puntual access to them, say, once per chapter?</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be my option. Principally for the reason that part of the Carthians' ethos (in their covenant book) is strong encouragement to do favours for one another without counting up debts. That's actually a pretty big plus compared to most covenants, particularly their main competitor. So mechanical representation of that is a good way to go.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, FWIW, I can get behind liking blood oaths but not Carthian Law in that I can easily see blood oaths being a refinement of the same process as the vinculum, whereas Carthian Law doesn't apparently follow from any existing part of the vampiric condition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T09:20:47-07:00","id":664454,"title":"","content":"I would be just as inclined to play a Carthian with<b>out</b> Law as an Invictus without Oaths. I think they are interesting, but I don't find them to be defining characteristics of the covenants. Cruac, Theban, and Coils are necessary to differentiate the covenants from the Invictus and Carthians. I'm not sure you need an alternative as much as a clear statement to players as to your intentions for Carthians in your game. If a player likes Carthians, but is wary of your intentions then you could bring that problem up, ask for solutions. There is no great universal answer, but there might be a great answer for your particular game. It won't be found without player input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":".  Didn't finish typing a word the first time. 09-14-2015, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T17:45:24-07:00","id":665100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/657585-2e-alternative-incentives-for-carthians?p=662487#post662487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, first, I'm not in love with the Invictus Oaths, but I find them workable. The main reason is that the Invictus Oaths are natural extensions of both the covenant fluff and the metaphysics shown in the setting - the Invictus are all about hierarchy and creating webs of social obligation, and they enforce that through the Blood. Like Cruac, Theban Sorcery, and the Coils/Scales, it all comes back to the Blood. I like that, that feels right and it falls in line with how the Kindred's more mystical powers have been shown to work.<br /> <br /> Carthian Law, meanwhile...doesn't. The clanbook gives a multiple choice reason why the magic works (and I don't like a single one) and the 2e core doesn't even touch on it, There's no reason why a bunch of vampires caring about the law gives it magical enforcement, and there's no reason why this power in particular only belongs to those vampires that call themselves &quot;Carthians&quot; - no one had the power before, and there's no explanation given why the newest, most secular covenant somehow developed a magic system of their own. On top of that, 2e takes a lot of effort to push the &quot;revolutionary&quot; aspects of the covenant, which makes it especially dissonant why they and only they are the power behind the laws of the domain. On top of THAT, I really don't like the effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually felt that Carthian Law could be tied back to the Blood in a way, similar to the Invictus theme you mention here. Whereas with Invictus Oaths, the Blood-bond is (I would say) the main thematic link, Carthian Law moves more to the tune of Blood Sympathy. The Invictus mindset spawns a blood &quot;magic&quot; that ties to its desire for structure, the Carthian mindset creates one that ties in to the idea of the consensus. This also would work to explain why only the Carthians can wield it, as it meta-physically &quot;needs&quot; a consensus of many. This might be just my interpretation of it however.<br /> <br /> That being said, while characters I have created tend towards the Ordo heavily, and I have yet to play in a game myself (the curse of being the only one willing to run a game in my area), I do think that, as a player, I would definitely feel that the Storyteller was more or less removing me from my part of in the spotlight. Not completely, obviously, but I am the kinda person that, if told that some of my potential cool toys were gone by the person running things, I'd be worried that I'm going to be the target, in some way, of future unfortunate story developments with little rhyme or reason (or fun for me). I do understand that those things should be brought up with the person running it, and that it probably doesn't happen that often in reality, but my observations with regards to others tends to lean to &quot;they'll do it a little, even if they don't realize it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Perhaps take a look at some of the more sabotage/disruption abilities of Demons, and homebrew some powers based on those for Carthians. They could be something as simple as Devotion-like powers that require the Carthian's radical touch, and some knowledge of how to get it to flow into the Blood, that spawned as a product of their anti-establishment-ish/revolutionary behavior and the need to survive against whoever is out to get them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cThe good sleep better, but the bad seem to enjoy the waking hours much more.\u201d</b> -<i>Woody Allen</i> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5322-zimthehacker","name":"Zimthehacker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5322_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T16:23:46-07:00","id":666128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/657585-2e-alternative-incentives-for-carthians?p=662487#post662487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Cruac, Theban Sorcery, and the Coils/Scales, it all comes back to the Blood. I like that, that feels right and it falls in line with how the Kindred's more mystical powers have been shown to work. Carthian Law, meanwhile...doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/657585-2e-alternative-incentives-for-carthians?p=664134#post664134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, FWIW, I can get behind liking blood oaths but not Carthian Law in that I can easily see blood oaths being a refinement of the same process as the vinculum, whereas Carthian Law doesn't apparently follow from any existing part of the vampiric condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This has always been my beef with Carthian Law- not mechanics, but metaphysics. All the other Covenants' superpowers are heavily vampire-themed- holy thaumaturgy, unholy blood sorcery, weird blasphemous evolution... but Carthian Law stands out as just &quot;nope, shared Kindred laws are a force of nature now&quot;.<br /> <br /> ...that said, I don't think there's any reason that Carthian Law <i>has </i>to break convention, or that it <i>can't</i> be explained using other, somewhat more subtle themes as Zim suggests (if for no other reason than if two editions and thousands of years of Kindred history have proved ANYTHING, it's that proper application of willpower and intent can make the Blood all but sit up and beg).<br /> <br /> If the Carthians were more tied into classical vampire themes... I feel like it'd take virtually just a single small alteration to make them feel <i>so </i>much more at home, in setting. Discuss blood sympathy as a supernatural basis for punishing those diverging from the Needs of the Many, as Zim said, or maybe develop a Carthian-specific model of the Beast that can be made to serve as a corrective hivemind rather than a competitive survivalist Id.<br /> <br /> Yum. Vampire Borg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:59:29-07:00","id":667263,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, Carthians are my go to covenant, because they are the bringers of social change to an otherwise fuedal mindset. Like the Ordo, the Carthians are unhappy with the world they have to live in and want to change it. Personally the law has always struck me as a bit off, but never metaphysically. I always pegged the power of their Law being something akin to creating a city 'bloodline&quot; through force of will and ideology. The Carthians say &quot;No Poaching!&quot; and their will, their beast, and their blood change the world, establishing the Law and a fitting punishment. Vitae is pure life force, and it can influence the entirety of the city, if you believe it can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}